<title>UK: UK to cut merchant shipping light dues in 1997/8.</title>
<headline>UK to cut merchant shipping light dues in 1997/8.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Light dues paid by merchant ships and fishing vessels in British waters will fall to 41 pence per net ton in 1997/8 from 43 pence in the current financial year, shipping minister Lord Goschen said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He said in a written parliamentary answer there would be consequential reduction in other charges.</p>
<p>Light dues fund the operation of lighthouses. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
